  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Aircraft Maintenance Technician A.S. Degree - CalGETC GE' program map, Catalog 2025-26, published January 27, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7000/PublishedPdf). GE Pattern: Cal-GETC. Official Total Units: 105-106; this seed models the first-listed/recommended path at the low end of variable-unit ranges = 5+17+17+17+17+3+16+13 = 105 units (ENGL C1000 at 3 units per the official SCC English course page). Semester sums verified against the map's 5 / 17 / 17 / 17 / 17 / 3 / 16-17 / 13 headers. The two Summer Terms are kept as their own terms (distinguished as First Year / Second Year) per the validator term-cap rule. AMTP 200 Certificated Aircraft Mechanic Preparation (1 unit) is a repeatable corequisite taken in each of Semesters 1-4; allow_repeated_courses is set and documented here. In-plan prereqs sequenced (all with grades of C or better): AMTP 200 & 300 require AMTP 309; AMTP 301 requires AMTP 309 + concurrent AMTP 300; AMTP 302 requires AMTP 300 & 301; AMTP 303 requires AMTP 300 & 301 + concurrent AMTP 302; AMTP 304 requires AMTP 302 & 303; AMTP 305 requires AMTP 302 & 303 + concurrent AMTP 304; AMTP 306 requires AMTP 304 & 305; AMTP 307 requires AMTP 304 & 305 + concurrent AMTP 306; AMTP 310 requires AMTP 309; AMTP 311 requires AMTP 309 + concurrent AMTP 310; AMTP 312 requires AMTP 310 & 311; AMTP 313 requires AMTP 310 & 311 + concurrent AMTP 312; AMTP 314 requires AMTP 312 & 313; AMTP 315 requires AMTP 312 & 313 + concurrent AMTP 314; AMTP 316 requires AMTP 314 & 315; AMTP 317 requires AMTP 314 & 315 + concurrent AMTP 316; AMTP 320/330 require AMTP 306, 307, 316 & 317; AMTP 321/331 require AMTP 306, 307, 316 & 317 + concurrent AMTP 320/330; AMTP 322/332 require AMTP 320 & 321 / AMTP 330 & 331; AMTP 323/333 require the same + concurrent AMTP 322/332; AMTP 324/334 require AMTP 322 & 323 / AMTP 332 & 333; AMTP 325/335 require the same + concurrent AMTP 324/334; AMTP 326/336 require AMTP 324 & 325 / AMTP 334 & 335; AMTP 327/337 require the same + concurrent AMTP 326/336. Semester corequisites with AMTP 200: S1: AMTP 300, 301, 303, 305, 307; S2: AMTP 311, 313, 315, 317; S3: AMTP 321, 323, 325, 327; S4: AMTP 331, 333, 335, 337 — concurrent AMTP 200 is included in those slots' prereq arrays. Choice slots: (1) ENGL C1000 (3) / ENGWR 488 / ESLW 340 (Area 1A; ENGWR 80/ENGL C1000 combo if not placing directly); (2) STAT C1000 (4) / STAT C1000H (Area 2; STAT 10/STAT C1000 combo if not placing directly). The Area 4 GE slot in Semester 6 must be from a different discipline than the Semester 5 Area 4 course (map note). The 1-unit Area 5C Associate Lab Component is modeled as printed; not required if a lab is included in 5A/5B. tccns mirrors SCC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS).",
